1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,102
A business brief should become a document a team can review, not a black box.

2
00:00:05,102 --> 00:00:11,397
One paragraph in, a reviewable DOCX out, with schema, validation and routing evidence attached.

3
00:00:11,397 --> 00:00:16,632
This is not a mock: the next scenes use a recorded live LLM plan and its trace.

4
00:00:16,632 --> 00:00:22,824
Here is a synthetic package with sample data, parser diagnostics and a normalized field tree.

5
00:00:22,824 --> 00:00:28,284
The schema is typed, so every field the document can bind has a type and a source.

6
00:00:28,284 --> 00:00:31,080
Nothing is invented from the prompt alone.

7
00:00:31,080 --> 00:00:37,789
The brief is the only input: plain language naming the fields, totals, VAT notice and footer.

8
00:00:37,789 --> 00:00:41,684
The planner turns each requirement into a typed field.

9
00:00:41,684 --> 00:00:43,632
No model is chosen by hand.

10
00:00:43,632 --> 00:00:45,357
The result is not prose.

11
00:00:45,357 --> 00:00:52,760
It is a Template IR: one section, sixteen typed blocks, a repeating line table and conditional notices.

12
00:00:52,760 --> 00:00:57,576
The same structure feeds validation, preview and the DOCX compiler.

13
00:00:57,576 --> 00:00:59,288
Auto does the choosing.

14
00:00:59,288 --> 00:01:05,021
It classifies the brief, recommends a provider, and sends no manual override.

15
00:01:05,021 --> 00:01:08,520
The decision is recorded before the model runs.

16
00:01:08,520 --> 00:01:12,623
The live run selected Anthropic and executed Claude Sonnet.

17
00:01:12,623 --> 00:01:19,368
Recommendation, execution, match and fallback are separate recorded facts, with a run identifier.

18
00:01:19,368 --> 00:01:21,387
The image family is typed too.

19
00:01:21,387 --> 00:01:31,080
A company logo, a schema image, or one product image per repeated line item use the same binding model, with explicit fallback and aspect ratio.

20
00:01:31,080 --> 00:01:37,333
Reference tables are read as geometry plus schema evidence: header, repeated row, footer total.

21
00:01:37,333 --> 00:01:42,336
Ambiguous and merged tables are refused with diagnostics instead of guessed.

22
00:01:42,336 --> 00:01:46,069
Reference evaluation is separate from semantic quality.

23
00:01:46,069 --> 00:01:51,092
Seventeen official documents parse, sixteen reach import, fifteen compile.

24
00:01:51,092 --> 00:01:57,744
Thirty tables are classified, and the two residual pipeline failures are named rather than hidden.

25
00:01:57,744 --> 00:02:02,360
The benchmark runs thirty-two cases across three providers and three repeats.

26
00:02:02,360 --> 00:02:11,712
Two hundred seventy-eight runs completed; two hundred seventy-four pass semantically, and ten Gemini technical failures are reported, not counted as passes.

27
00:02:11,712 --> 00:02:13,543
Download and open the file.

28
00:02:13,543 --> 00:02:21,407
The preview and the LibreOffice render are independent views of the same document, each labelled for what it proves.

29
00:02:21,407 --> 00:02:23,712
This is not a Word fidelity claim.

30
00:02:23,712 --> 00:02:27,024
Docentric Copilot is open source under Apache.

31
00:02:27,024 --> 00:02:33,720
The schema, the live decision, the typed template and the evidence are all in the repository.

32
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:36,672
Docentric AX compatibility is not tested.
